G1411.def:
δύναμις, -εως, ἡ 
(δύναμαι), [in LXX for עֹז ,גּבוּרָה ,צָבָה ,(חֵיל) חַיִל, etc.; 35 words in all ;] 
power, might, strength; relatively, ability, power to perform: Matthieu 25:15, Actes 3:12, Hébreux 11:11; κατὰ δ., 2 Corinthiens 8:3; παρὰ δ., ib.; ὑπὲρ δ., 2 Corinthiens 1:8; of pecuniary ability, 2 Corinthiens 8:3, Apocalypse 18:3; absol., power, might: Luc 24:49, Actes 1:8; opposite to ἀσθένεια, 1 Corinthiens 15:43; ἡ δ. τ. ἁμαρτίας, 1 Corinthiens 15:56; of power in action, Romains 1:16, 20 1 Corinthiens 1:18, Philippiens 3:10, al.; ἡ δ. τ. θεοῦ, Matthieu 22:29, Marc 12:24, Romains 1:20, al.; opposite to μόρφωσις, 2 Timothée 3:5; in doxologies, Apocalypse 4:11 7:12, al.; ἐν δ., Marc 9:1, Luc 4:36, Romains 1:4, al.; of the power of performing miracles, Actes 6:8, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:9; pl., Matthieu 13:54, Marc 6:14, Galates 3:5, al.; of the force or meaning of a word (Plat., al.), 1 Corinthiens 14:11. By meton., of persons or things; 
__(a) of God, Matthieu 26:64, Marc 14:62 (Dalman, Words, 200ff.); 
__(b) of angels, Romains 8:38, Éphésiens 1:21, 1 Pierre 3:22; 
__(with) of armies, pl. [LXX for צְבָאוֹת ], metaphorically, of the stars, Matthieu 24:29, Marc 13:25, Luc 21:26; 
__(d) of that wh. manifests God's power: Christ, 1 Corinthiens 1:24; τ. εὐαγγέλλιον, Romains 1:16; ἡ δ. τ. κυρίου, 1 Corinthiens 5:4; 
__(e) of mighty works (Tr., Syn., §xci), δ. ποιεῖν, Marc 6:5 9:39; pl., Matthieu 7:22, Marc 6:2, Luc 10:13, al.; σημεῖακ. δ., Actes 8:13; δ. κ. τέρατα κ. σημεῖα, Actes 2:22, 2 Corinthiens 12:12. 
SYN.: βία, ἐνέργεια, ἐξουσία, ἰσχύς, κράτος (see Tr., l.with; Cremer, 218, 236; DB, i, 616; iv, 29; DCG, i, 607; ii, 188).

G1437.def:
ἐάν, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν, 
conditional particle, 
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. Jean 13:17, 1 Corinthiens 7:36), if haply, if; 
__1. with subjc. (cl.); 
__(a) pres.: Matthieu 6:22, Luc 10:6, Jean 7:17, Romains 2:25, 26 al.; 
{ __(b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): Matthieu 4:9 16:26 (cf. ptcp. in Luc 9:25; M, Pr., 230), Marc 3:24, Luc 14:34, Jean 5:43, Romains 7:2, al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., Jean 9:22 11:57, Actes 9:2; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, Jean 12:32 14:3, I Jean 2:28 3:2, Hébreux 3:7" (LXX) . 
__2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, App., 171; VD, MGr. 2, App., §77; Deiss., BS, 201f., LAE, 155, 254; M, Pr., 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4); 
__(a) fut.: Matthieu 18:19 T, Luc 19:40, Actes 7:7; 
__(b) pres.: 1 Thessaloniciens 3:8 (see Milligan, in l.). 
__3. With other particles: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), Galates 6:1; ἐ. μή (M, Pr., 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., Matthieu 10:13, 1 Corinthiens 8:8, Jacques 2:17, 1 Jean 3:21; aor., Matthieu 6:15, Marc 3:27, Jean 3:3, Romains 10:15, Galates 1:8 2:16 (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, Esther 19:13, al.,] Romains 14:8. 
__4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., Pr., 96; WH, App., 173; M, Pr., 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., BS, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., Matthieu 5:19, Marc 6:22, 23 Luc 17:32, 1 Corinthiens 6:18, al.; ὅπου ἐ., Matthieu 8:19; ὁσάκις ἐ., Apocalypse 11:6; οὗ ἐ., 1 Corinthiens 16:6; καθὸ ἐ., 2 Corinthiens 8:12; ὅστις ἐ., Galates 5:10.

G1438.def:
ἑαυτοῦ, -ῆς, -οῦ, dative -ῷ, etc., accusative -όν, etc., pi. -ῶν, etc. (Att. contr. αὑτοῦ, etc); 
reflex pron.; 
__1. prop, of 3rd person (Lat. sui, sibi, se), of himself, herself, itself, etc.: Matthieu 27:42, Marc 15:31, Luc 23:35, al.; added to a middle verb, διεμερίσαντο ἑαυτοῖς, Jean 19:24; to an active verb, Actes 14:14 (M, Pr., 157); ἀφ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, Luc 12:57 21:30, Jean 5:19, al. (see: ἀπό); δι᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, Romains 14:14; ἐν ἑ., Matthieu 3:9, Marc 5:30, al.; εἰς ἑ., Luc 15:17; καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, Actes 28:16, Jacques 2:17; παρ᾽ ἑαυτῷ, at his own house, 1 Corinthiens 16:2; πρὸς ἑ., with, to himself, Luc 18:11; as poss. pron. (with emphasis weakened; see M, Pr., 87f.), τ. ἑαυτῶν νεκρούς, Luc 9:60. 
__2. As reflexive 1st and 2nd of person(s) (so also frequently in cl., chiefly poetry), Matthieu 23:31, Marc 9:50, Romains 8:23, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:8, al. 
__3. In pl., for reciprocal pron., ἀλλήλων, -οις, -ους, of one another, etc.: Matthieu 21:38, Marc 16:3, Éphésiens 5:19, al.

G1464.def:
ἐγκοπή, see: ἐνκ-.
ἐν-κοπή (Rec. ἐγκ-, see: ἐν; T, ἐκκ-), -ῆς, ἡ (ἐγκόπτω) ; 
1. an incision, a cutting, break. 2. Metaphorical, an interruption, a hindrance: 1 Corinthiens 9:12.†

G1465.def:
ἐγκόπτω, see: ἐνκ-.
ἐν-κόπτω (Rec. ἐγκ-, see: ἐν; and in I Pe, l.with, ἐκκ-); 
1. to cut into (as in breaking up a road), hence, 2. to hinder: with accusative Actes 24:4, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:18, . inf., Galates 5:7; before τοῦ, with inf., Romains 15:22; εἰς τό, with inf, 1 Pierre 3:7.†
